{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1385381-v20-retainer-dots-and-ghoul-creation","id":1385381,"title":"[V20] Retainer Dots and Ghoul Creation","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-05-03T02:33:11-07:00","id":1385381,"title":"[V20] Retainer Dots and Ghoul Creation","content":"So my ST has decided that she wants to transfer over to using V20 once our current V5 game/story is over.<br /> We (PCs) would likely have to rebuild our characters from scratch using the V20 system.<br /> <br /> I'm checking up on some character related rules for V20, so that I can be prepared for the change.<br /> <br /> My character has a ghoul, one that has followed him for centuries.<br /> In V5, my ST have my character put more advantage points into retainer, to make for a more power ghoul. (He uses a more powerful human stats array)<br /> *Powerful/Stronger here and below, means having a ghoul that has more skills, stats, merit, advantage etc then a normal ghoul. Not necessarily stronger physically.<br /> <br /> In V20, I understand that each dot in retainer gives 1 extra ghoul, but you can also ask your ST to allow you to make stronger ghouls by investing more dots into a single ghoul.<br /> Also in V20, ghouls have actual rules for character creation. With some additional rules for older ghouls, like able to hold more BP.<br /> <br /> Given that more dots in a Retainer allows you to making a stronger ghoul, how does this work in V20?<br /> Does such a ghoul get more xp at the start? Get better starting stats?<br /> <br /> How does more dots in Retainer correspond to have a stronger ghoul in V20.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26067,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26067-wingstorm","user":"Wingstorm","date":".  Fixed some typos 05-03-2020, 11:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26067-wingstorm","name":"Wingstorm","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-03T05:25:31-07:00","id":1385389,"title":"","content":"The official answer is &quot;Talk to your Storyteller.&quot;<br /> <br /> My house rule though, based on the old familiar rules for Mage, is that they get 10 extra freebie points per dot you spend on them.<br /> <br /> For comparison, buying up the two attribute dots, five skill dots and one discipline dot that separates a starting vampire from a starting ghoul costs 30 freebie points.* Thus, a ghoul about as tough as a starting vampire would take four dots in retainers (one for the base ghoul, three more for +30 freebie points).<br /> <br /> * For simplicity, I consider the &quot;can move around in the day and extra freebies vs. more fragile, limited discipline access (normally limited rank one and costs 10 freebie/20 XP to acquire) and low blood pool (2 points in V20) to be a wash.<br /> <br /> ETA: I don't bother with assigning a freebie point value to a larger blood pool for ghouls because, per the rules, it only increases by one point every 200 years as a ghoul. Few starting PCs are even going to be 200 years old themselves, much less have a ghoul that's 220+ years old.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1328,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","user":"Chris24601","date":". 05-03-2020, 08:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-03T10:45:04-07:00","id":1385431,"title":"","content":"Yes, you can put more points into a more powerful retainer in V20 at storyteller's discretion. How many dots? over 3 would be excessive for anyone but an elder. If you've put a lot into it (as v5 bacgrounds are mostly weaker) I'd just reallocate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-03T20:00:57-07:00","id":1385523,"title":"","content":"Well, the ghoul in question is around 800~900 years old.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26067-wingstorm","name":"Wingstorm","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-20T08:10:22-07:00","id":1390290,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1385381-v20-retainer-dots-and-ghoul-creation?p=1385389#post1385389\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The official answer is &amp;quot;Talk to your Storyteller.&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> My house rule though, based on the old familiar rules for Mage, is that they get 10 extra freebie points per dot you spend on them.<br /> <br /> For comparison, buying up the two attribute dots, five skill dots and one discipline dot that separates a starting vampire from a starting ghoul costs 30 freebie points.* Thus, a ghoul about as tough as a starting vampire would take four dots in retainers (one for the base ghoul, three more for +30 freebie points).<br /> <br /> * For simplicity, I consider the &amp;quot;can move around in the day and extra freebies vs. more fragile, limited discipline access (normally limited rank one and costs 10 freebie/20 XP to acquire) and low blood pool (2 points in V20) to be a wash.<br /> <br /> ETA: I don't bother with assigning a freebie point value to a larger blood pool for ghouls because, per the rules, it only increases by one point every 200 years as a ghoul. Few starting PCs are even going to be 200 years old themselves, much less have a ghoul that's 220+ years old.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for this suggestion. I showed it to my ST and she plans to use it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26067-wingstorm","name":"Wingstorm","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}